Every time she would talk about me going,
and even when I was saying goodbye to

01:36:37.750 --> 01:36:39.574
them, she couldn't stop crying.

01:36:39.880 --> 01:36:40.998
And I thought, what

01:36:42.620 --> 01:36:48.440
And then my brother, when he was, he was a
missions pastor at the church I was being

01:36:48.440 --> 01:36:49.140
sent from,

01:36:49.760 --> 01:36:51.060
and he

01:36:52.740 --> 01:36:53.440
wrong

01:36:56.240 --> 01:36:59.620
with you? And if you need me, whatever it
is, you just call me.

01:36:59.620 --> 01:37:01.820
I'll be there. I'll take me three days to
get there, but I'll get there.

01:37:01.820 --> 01:37:04.900
You just call me. I'll get, and I'm like,
what is he going on about?

01:37:04.900 --> 01:37:07.260
And he's like, I don't want, I don't know
if I could do this.

01:37:07.260 --> 01:37:08.680
I don't know if I can put you on that bus.

01:37:08.680 --> 01:37:10.080
I don't know if I could do this.

01:37:10.080 --> 01:37:12.100
And I was just like, these people are
crazy.

01:37:12.100 --> 01:37:13.276
Like they're insane.

01:37:13.800 --> 01:37:15.000
And but I'm going right.

01:37:15.000 --> 01:37:19.230
So I get on that And And I thought about
it a couple times, but I remember people

01:37:19.230 --> 01:37:22.210
said, it's going to be hardest trip that
I've ever been on, but God's going to be

01:37:22.210 --> 01:37:24.610
with me and, um, and I kept.

01:37:24.660 --> 01:37:27.800
wondering what is, what is, you know, what
is this about?

01:37:27.800 --> 01:37:29.624
And but I kind of put it aside,

01:37:30.540 --> 01:37:35.120
and I went on the trip from the very
beginning of the trip, I got malaria.

01:37:36.480 --> 01:37:40.160
And malaria, just like if you can think of
any other disease, even like COVID, you

01:37:40.160 --> 01:37:43.660
can have the disease for a little while
before you show signs of the disease.

01:37:43.660 --> 01:37:44.660
Typically,

01:37:45.420 --> 01:37:50.080
the symptoms that kind of tell that it's
COVID, or sorry, not COVID, that it's

01:37:50.080 --> 01:37:54.280
malaria take about two It could be a
little bit sooner, but it takes about two

01:37:54.280 --> 01:37:56.221
weeks to know that it is malaria.

01:37:56.720 --> 01:38:01.073
Now unlike COVID, malaria you can't give
to someone else during that time.

01:38:03.444 --> 01:38:08.244
So, I had malaria, but because I had
malaria, my body was very weak, so I

01:38:08.244 --> 01:38:10.244
started getting all these other...

01:38:11.026 --> 01:38:14.886
other things and some weird symptoms came
up, like for example, sensitivity.

01:38:14.886 --> 01:38:16.920
Sensitivity to touch and to pain.

01:38:18.280 --> 01:38:22.980
We would oftentimes when you're, you know,
if you don't have a proper shower for

01:38:22.980 --> 01:38:26.900
quite a while, we would braid our hair or
put our hair up.

01:38:27.120 --> 01:38:29.500
And we'd often braid it because then it
looked a little bit cuter.

01:38:29.500 --> 01:38:32.900
And so we'd all help each other braid each
other's hair.

01:38:33.140 --> 01:38:34.440
And some girls are braiding my hair.

01:38:34.440 --> 01:38:36.969
It felt like they were yanking my hair
out.

01:38:37.160 --> 01:38:38.780
And I just said, can you go softer?

01:38:38.780 --> 01:38:42.940
Can you go softer? And they were basically
just like doing this with my hair, but it

01:38:42.940 --> 01:38:46.780
still felt like they're pulling my hair
on, like something's wrong, something's

01:38:46.780 --> 01:38:50.100
not. But I just kept like getting sick
over and over again, but we didn't know

01:38:50.100 --> 01:38:54.571
yet it was malaria because the typical
malaria symptoms hadn't come out yet.

01:38:54.670 --> 01:38:57.846
And so I ended up, I haven't found out it
was malaria.

01:38:57.930 --> 01:39:01.940
I had stomach bacteria, strep throat.

01:39:03.080 --> 01:39:04.820
Both of my eardrums had ruptured.

01:39:04.820 --> 01:39:06.000
Had ear infections.

01:39:07.480 --> 01:39:11.320
I was just a mess. I had the bites of my,
I had so many bites.

01:39:11.460 --> 01:39:13.680
They're all infected all over my body.

01:39:13.680 --> 01:39:15.960
And so very sick before I found out.

01:39:16.060 --> 01:39:21.700
I'd also, in getting to a village, we had
a hike into the villages and hiking.

01:39:21.880 --> 01:39:26.860
I was hiking down the mountain, but my,
literally we went up and over mountains.

01:39:28.900 --> 01:39:34.590
And the fevers, one of the symptoms of
malaria is that you have fevers that you

01:39:34.590 --> 01:39:38.790
just go in.. And I had fevers and I had my
fevers spiked.

01:39:39.590 --> 01:39:43.178
So hot that it was uncomfortable for
anyone to touch my skin.

01:39:43.310 --> 01:39:46.270
I was so hot that it was uncomfortable for
anyone to touch my skin.

01:39:46.270 --> 01:39:51.211
So I don't even know how I was, I mean, I
know how I was alive, basically just Jesus

01:39:51.330 --> 01:39:53.448
because I shouldn't have been alive.

01:39:53.450 --> 01:39:56.750
But I was so hot that my body, in
Indonesia,

01:39:58.040 --> 01:40:04.410
the humidity is so high that the sweat on
your skin doesn't

01:40:04.410 --> 01:40:06.234
evaporate. It just stays there.

01:40:06.280 --> 01:40:09.398
So all of this, my body was sweating from
the fevers.

01:40:09.780 --> 01:40:13.240
My body was sweating from hiking up over
mountains.

01:40:13.900 --> 01:40:19.840
And so my body was so hot and all of the
moisture was still on my skin and it was

01:40:19.840 --> 01:40:21.760
like rainy and wet anyway

01:40:22.880 --> 01:40:26.645
that I had heat stroke and I fainted and
slid down the mountain.

01:40:27.600 --> 01:40:32.080
And then it was like my body, ata that
moment, my body completely shut down.

01:40:32.400 --> 01:40:34.360
I couldn't go to the bathroom for three
days.

01:40:34.360 --> 01:40:39.120
What happens when you're that severely
sick, your body will start shutting down

01:40:39.120 --> 01:40:40.680
things it doesn't need to survive.

01:40:40.680 --> 01:40:45.700
And it didn't need to digest food and it
didn't need to go to the bathroom.

01:40:45.960 --> 01:40:47.725
It was just trying to survive.

01:40:48.140 --> 01:40:51.000
And so I was hot to touch for several
days.

01:40:51.460 --> 01:40:54.920
So it was just, I mean, it was like
hardship after hardship, right?

01:40:54.920 --> 01:40:56.660
And this happened for weeks.

01:40:56.660 --> 01:40:58.160
So here I, I am

01:40:58.950 --> 01:41:02.230
the senior leader on this trip, super
sick,

01:41:03.050 --> 01:41:03.750
super

01:41:05.140 --> 01:41:07.260
just not, not doing good at all.

01:41:07.380 --> 01:41:09.900
I mean, it really was the hardest trip I'd
ever had.

01:41:09.900 --> 01:41:13.380
You know, came close to death so many
times during that time with malaria.

01:41:13.380 --> 01:41:17.300
But meanwhile, here in the States, three
people that God had spoken to,

01:41:17.300 --> 01:41:19.500
well, Tamara will still love me.

01:41:20.610 --> 01:41:25.050
One night when I was dying of malaria,
this is when I had all of those other

01:41:25.050 --> 01:41:29.140
sicknesses, but I'm literally dying of
malaria that the village leader comes in

01:41:29.140 --> 01:41:30.520
and says that she doesn't get help.

01:41:30.520 --> 01:41:32.108
She's going to die tonight.

01:41:32.300 --> 01:41:34.600
And, you know, they worked it out.

01:41:34.600 --> 01:41:37.960
It was a true miracle that they got me out
of the village.

01:41:37.960 --> 01:41:41.901
There was a motorcyclist who was coming
through that then got help.

01:41:42.060 --> 01:41:47.490
And, you know, I really believe it was an
angel who drove that truck into, through

01:41:47.490 --> 01:41:49.630
the jungle, drove this, you know,,

01:41:51.010 --> 01:41:55.700
sipped out really nice truck in the middle
of nowhere in Indonesia, drove it through

01:41:55.700 --> 01:41:58.600
the jungle to pick me up and take me to
the nearest hospital

01:41:58.600 --> 01:42:01.940
and was able to get the medical help and
attention I needed.

01:42:01.940 --> 01:42:04.360
I was so dehydrated. I was so,

01:42:05.460 --> 01:42:09.160
they tried to get me me to take medication
and I couldn't get it down.

01:42:09.160 --> 01:42:14.080
I just kept throwing it up so they would
have to put IVs in just to get enough

01:42:14.080 --> 01:42:16.727
fluids in. So it was a pretty miserable
time,

01:42:16.840 --> 01:42:20.980
a miserable trip. But. I remember just
lying in the hospital that night and

01:42:20.980 --> 01:42:26.600
before that when I was dying in the
village, just lying there and this moment

01:42:26.600 --> 01:42:32.940
where I was throwing up nonstop and I just
had nothing else to throw up, but I kept

01:42:32.940 --> 01:42:34.587
throwing up and dry heaving.

01:42:35.970 --> 01:42:40.950
And I had this moment, had a brief respite
for a couple of minutes, and I laid down

01:42:40.950 --> 01:42:43.715
and I thought, this is it, this is where I
got.

01:42:43.980 --> 01:42:45.804
And I thought, you know, Jesus,

01:42:46.180 --> 01:42:48.768
even if this is it, even if this is the
end,

01:42:49.500 --> 01:42:55.920
and it's all worth it. And to get to that
moment to say that, I don't say that

01:42:55.920 --> 01:43:00.780
because of how great I am, but only
because I feel like knowing the hardship

01:43:00.780 --> 01:43:05.510
that was going to come. I wrapped my mind
around, you know, it's going to be hard,

01:43:05.510 --> 01:43:06.430
but it's okay.

01:43:07.820 --> 01:43:09.900
It's worth it. Jesus is enough.

01:43:10.340 --> 01:43:15.164
God is enough. And how much better to die
in this place doing the will of the Lord

01:43:15.500 --> 01:43:20.310
than to die doing my own selfish desires,
right?

01:43:20.410 --> 01:43:23.730
So I just had such peace that came over me
in that moment.

01:43:23.730 --> 01:43:26.170
And in the hospital, I just had such
peace.

01:43:26.170 --> 01:43:30.170
Knowing that it was going to be hard gave
me the peace to get through it and the

01:43:30.170 --> 01:43:31.290
strength to get through it.

01:43:31.290 --> 01:43:36.670
And, you know, that same night here in the
States, those three people, God woke up.

01:43:38.260 --> 01:43:39.240
So today now,

01:43:40.120 --> 01:43:43.880
during the day when the leader said,
tonight she's going to die, it was night

01:43:43.880 --> 01:43:46.640
here in the States. God woke those three
people up.

01:43:46.640 --> 01:43:50.060
One of them had been my sister who ran
into my parents room and said, woke up my

01:43:50.060 --> 01:43:52.280
parents and said, Tamara is dying right
now.

01:43:52.280 --> 01:43:53.692
We need to pray for her.

01:43:54.370 --> 01:43:58.670
And my whole family got some friends to
get up, leaders to get out across

01:44:00.010 --> 01:44:01.910
California in the US to start praying for
me.

01:44:01.910 --> 01:44:04.670
And they all stayed up all night long
praying.

01:44:05.690 --> 01:44:09.980
and, you know, can you just imagine the
fear that my mother, you know, just the

01:44:09.980 --> 01:44:12.686
fear of a mom just sitting and thinking
these,

01:44:13.300 --> 01:44:16.920
she may not come home. She's dying right
now and to pray.

01:44:17.300 --> 01:44:20.950
But what that experience did hardship and,
you know,

01:44:21.590 --> 01:44:23.210
to finish off the story,

01:44:24.270 --> 01:44:28.600
it was still, I actually didn't get
medical attention for another two weeks

01:44:28.600 --> 01:44:32.060
before I got the proper medical attention
because the hospital I was at didn't have

01:44:32.060 --> 01:44:33.060
an adequate help.

01:44:33.660 --> 01:44:35.954
So I still got even sicker before I was

01:44:36.500 --> 01:44:39.260
truly got what I needed.

01:44:39.700 --> 01:44:43.746
When I got out of the village, they had
talked to the church leaders that picked

01:44:43.746 --> 01:44:48.786
us up from the boats that had taken us to
the village area.

01:44:49.458 --> 01:44:53.498
The church leaders, they told the church
leaders she needs to go directly to a

01:44:53.498 --> 01:44:54.198
hospital.

01:44:54.638 --> 01:44:59.418
So they picked me up, literally the rest
of the team went on to their home stay,

01:44:59.718 --> 01:45:01.878
but I was picked up and taken straight to
the hospital.

01:45:01.878 --> 01:45:03.878
They took my blood. blood samples.

01:45:04.570 --> 01:45:07.850
And the texts that were taking the blood,

01:45:08.870 --> 01:45:13.000
they looked at me when they had the
results, they looked at me and they said,

01:45:13.000 --> 01:45:14.765
I don't know how you're alive.

01:45:15.290 --> 01:45:18.510
This is this blood dead person.

01:45:19.400 --> 01:45:24.270
What that doesn't make sense that I if I
didn't know that I just took your blood

01:45:24.270 --> 01:45:27.650
and just now tested, I would think that
this was a corpse blood.

01:45:27.650 --> 01:45:28.474
Like it's not,

01:45:29.200 --> 01:45:31.780
this is not a human being's blood that's
living.

01:45:31.780 --> 01:45:32.545
So they said,

01:45:33.500 --> 01:45:34.200
So sick.

01:45:35.070 --> 01:45:39.050
And when I saw the doctor after that, he
looked at it, he said the same thing.

01:45:39.050 --> 01:45:43.521
And he said, well, you've got and he
started listing everything that I have.

01:45:44.560 --> 01:45:49.880
And he did tests after tests, even when he
took my hearing test, I lost several,

01:45:50.480 --> 01:45:54.880
I still to this day have some hearing loss
from the rupture of ultimate eardrums

01:45:54.880 --> 01:45:57.233
rupture. And he took pictures of it all.

01:45:57.340 --> 01:45:58.700
It just was, he's like,

01:45:59.540 --> 01:46:03.250
I don't know how you're standing in front
of me, right?

01:46:03.370 --> 01:46:07.330
In a straight, but I don't even know how
you're alive right now.

01:46:07.940 --> 01:46:10.560
But he gave me all these medications to
help me.

01:46:10.560 --> 01:46:14.420
And it took a couple months actually to
fully get better and to get my strength

01:46:14.420 --> 01:46:19.680
back. But that experience and going
through for me, I felt like I came so much

01:46:19.680 --> 01:46:22.480
closer to Jesus, than I'd ever been before
through that hardship.

01:46:22.480 --> 01:46:26.740
But it was knowing that the persecution
was coming, that I was able to get my mind

01:46:26.740 --> 01:46:28.740
wrapped around it. So I didn't

01:46:29.360 --> 01:46:30.700
just be

01:46:35.400 --> 01:46:38.260
had no clue who knew that I was dying.

01:46:38.760 --> 01:46:45.260
It gave them the desire and the motivation
to pray and to seek the

01:46:45.260 --> 01:46:45.960
Lord.

01:46:46.060 --> 01:46:49.820
But my mom talks about to this day, that
memory, she still cries when she talks

01:46:49.820 --> 01:46:54.291
about it. But she talks about how she had
a renewed relationship with Jesus.

01:46:54.560 --> 01:46:57.680
With that idea, when Jesus asked her,
would you still love me even if I took

01:46:57.680 --> 01:47:01.720
your daughter from you? That she talks
about her faith and her journey with God

01:47:01.720 --> 01:47:03.073
being so much stronger.

01:47:06.040 --> 01:47:11.380
To encourage us that persecution can be
something that can bring us closer to

01:47:11.380 --> 01:47:16.360
Jesus, could make us stronger, could make
us more mature in the Lord, can lead

01:47:16.360 --> 01:47:19.740
people towards maturity, can lead people
towards Christ.

01:47:20.340 --> 01:47:24.520
But ultimately, to remember that we are
not alone, that even if it's the end, even

01:47:24.520 --> 01:47:25.344
if it's death,

01:47:25.960 --> 01:47:29.020
that the life of God is still worth it.

01:47:29.900 --> 01:47:35.660
And to have said that, to have known that,
has given me now so much more peace

01:47:37.060 --> 01:47:41.000
I moved in with a friend after that, the
story.

01:47:41.200 --> 01:47:41.900
And she,

01:47:42.320 --> 01:47:45.760
she was very, very scared of two girls
living on her own.

01:47:45.840 --> 01:47:49.880
And she would always be like, I forget to
lock the door or every night she want to

01:47:49.880 --> 01:47:53.760
put the blinds down. And I just, one day I
said, why do you do that?

01:47:53.760 --> 01:47:56.220
And she said, I'm so worried about safety.

01:47:56.220 --> 01:48:01.670
And after after this, this whole moment
with a near death, I just said to her,

01:48:02.090 --> 01:48:06.550
God's got us. You know, if something
happens, he's going to take care of us.

01:48:06.550 --> 01:48:10.844
You know, and I just had such strength in
that belief and faith in Jesus.

01:48:10.930 --> 01:48:15.470
And I really can say that it came from
mostly from the moment of even at the end

01:48:15.470 --> 01:48:17.176
saying it was still worth it.

01:48:17.330 --> 01:48:18.870
And so knowing persecution

01:48:19.470 --> 01:48:21.630
builds us up, persecution makes us.

01:48:21.730 --> 01:48:26.710
I truly believe that Paul was such a
strong, mature Christian because of all

01:48:26.710 --> 01:48:31.860
the persecution that he went through and
the words of wisdom that he has, that he

01:48:31.860 --> 01:48:33.400
has left the church with.

01:48:33.400 --> 01:48:38.580
I truly believe it came, the wisdom came
through all the persecution he went

01:48:38.980 --> 01:48:39.940
through.

01:48:42.810 --> 01:48:45.045
So persecution can have an importance.

01:48:46.770 --> 01:48:47.535
Any thoughts?

01:48:54.000 --> 01:48:57.520
That was such an amazing, amazing story
story Tamra.

01:48:57.760 --> 01:48:59.440
Just like so overcome.

01:49:00.480 --> 01:49:04.320
You know, I'm just crying, just hearing
all that you experienced and the strength

01:49:04.320 --> 01:49:06.980
that you found and you know, your family.

01:49:07.460 --> 01:49:10.420
And there was so much truth in what you're
saying.

01:49:10.420 --> 01:49:14.040
And I just appreciate that you shared all
of that with us.

01:49:14.200 --> 01:49:14.906
I thank you.

01:49:15.960 --> 01:49:17.078
Yeah, that is good.

01:49:18.520 --> 01:49:20.814
It's good to be sovereign in our lives.

01:49:22.994 --> 01:49:27.314
I think it's something we can remember
even in this time, this scary time, with

01:49:27.314 --> 01:49:31.674
my family just going through this COVID
scare and not knowing if my brother -in

01:49:31.674 --> 01:49:33.968
-law would come home from the hospital.

01:49:36.310 --> 01:49:39.370
I think it's something we if her husband
was going to come home there, and the

01:49:39.370 --> 01:49:45.770
process of the little girl who's one years
old, and just the fear

01:49:45.770 --> 01:49:50.100
of he could leave me with, you know, three
children and all of that.

01:49:50.400 --> 01:49:52.080
But God is God is sovereign.

01:49:52.880 --> 01:49:57.240
And he can get you not saying that bad
things won't happen.

01:49:58.080 --> 01:50:00.180
Not saying that it won't be the end.

01:50:00.180 --> 01:50:00.880
You know,

01:50:01.500 --> 01:50:03.147
when I lost my little sister

01:50:03.540 --> 01:50:04.860
and she went to be with Jesus.

01:50:04.860 --> 01:50:07.220
It was like, how could God do this?

01:50:07.260 --> 01:50:08.789
How could he take a child?

01:50:09.370 --> 01:50:13.340
Whether or not we know the answers, we
still can know that God is sovereign and

01:50:13.340 --> 01:50:15.400
that God knows the best for us.

