02:16:22.510 --> 02:16:25.039
Three days before arriving in the
province,

02:16:25.400 --> 02:16:29.420
a fastest went up from Caesarea to
Jerusalem Jerusalem, where the chief

02:16:29.420 --> 02:16:32.420
priests and the Jewish leaders appeared
before him.

02:16:32.560 --> 02:16:34.700
presented the charges against Paul.

02:16:35.900 --> 02:16:40.560
They requested Festus as a favor to them
to have Paul transferred to Jerusalem,

02:16:40.720 --> 02:16:44.760
where they were preparing an ambush to
kill himritical along the way.

02:16:44.760 --> 02:16:51.180
Festus answered, Paul is being held in
Caesarea and I myself am going there soon.

02:16:51.780 --> 02:16:56.540
Let some of your leaders come with me and
if the man has done anything wrong, they

02:16:56.540 --> 02:16:58.658
can press charges against him there.

02:16:59.280 --> 02:17:04.920
After spending eight or 10 days with them,
Festus went down to Caesarea.

02:17:05.820 --> 02:17:10.800
The next day, he convened the court and
ordered that Paul be brought before him.

02:17:11.430 --> 02:17:16.910
When Paul came in, the Jews who had come
down from Jerusalem stood around him.

02:17:17.510 --> 02:17:22.039
They brought many serious charges against
him, but they could not prove them.

02:17:22.410 --> 02:17:26.910
Then Paul made his defense, I have done
nothing wrong, against Jewish law or

02:17:26.910 --> 02:17:29.086
against the temple or against Caesar.

02:17:30.450 --> 02:17:35.510
Festus, wishing to do the Jews a favor,
said to Paul, are you willing to go up to

02:17:35.510 --> 02:17:36.210
Jerusalem

02:17:36.490 --> 02:17:39.990
and stand trial before me there on these
charges?

02:17:40.930 --> 02:17:46.210
Paul answered, I am now standing before
Caesar's court where I ought to be tried.

02:17:46.940 --> 02:17:52.040
I have not done anything wrong to the
Jews, as you yourself, very well known,

02:17:53.430 --> 02:17:54.312
know very well.

02:17:55.150 --> 02:18:00.170
If, however, I am guilty of doing anything
deserving death, I do not refuse to die.

02:18:00.450 --> 02:18:04.274
But if the charges brought against me by
these Jews are not true,

02:18:04.710 --> 02:18:07.357
no one has the right to hand me over to
them,

02:18:07.750 --> 02:18:10.950
I appeal to Caesar.

02:18:11.610 --> 02:18:17.340
After Festus had conferred to his council,
he declared,

02:18:17.960 --> 02:18:21.220
you have appealed to Caesar, to Caesar you
will go.

02:18:22.070 --> 02:18:27.250
A few days later, King Agrippa and Bernice
arrived at Caesarea to pay their respects

02:18:27.250 --> 02:18:27.950
to Festus.

02:18:28.610 --> 02:18:33.190
Since they were spending many days there,
Festus discussed Paul's case with the

02:18:33.190 --> 02:18:38.826
king., He said, there is a man here who
best who Felix left as a prisoner.

02:18:39.360 --> 02:18:45.840
He brought charges against him and asked
that he be condemned.

02:18:47.320 --> 02:18:53.570
I told him, I told them that it is not the
road of Roman custom to hand over anyone

02:18:53.570 --> 02:18:55.688
before they have faced their abuses,

02:18:55.930 --> 02:19:01.010
have gone and have had the opportunity to
defend themselves against the charges.

02:19:02.000 --> 02:19:06.240
When they came here with us, I did not
delay the case but convened the court.

02:19:06.240 --> 02:19:10.310
And the next day I ordered the man be
brought in.

02:19:12.460 --> 02:19:18.340
When his charges, when his accusers got up
to speak, they did not charge him with any

02:19:18.340 --> 02:19:20.046
of the crimes I had expected.

02:19:20.600 --> 02:19:26.440
Instead, they had some points of dispute
with him about their own religion and

02:19:26.440 --> 02:19:30.280
about a dead man named Jesus who Paul
claimed was alive.

02:19:30.930 --> 02:19:33.890
I was at a loss to investigate such
matters.

02:19:34.540 --> 02:19:40.480
So I asked if he would be willing to go to
Jerusalem and stand trial there on these

02:19:40.480 --> 02:19:41.180
charges.

02:19:41.660 --> 02:19:47.930
But when Paul made, his appeal to be held
over for the emperor's decision, I ordered

02:19:47.930 --> 02:19:51.090
him to be held until I could send him to
Caesar.

02:19:52.820 --> 02:19:57.080
Then Agrippa said to Festus, I would like
to hear this man myself.

02:19:57.660 --> 02:19:58.480
He replied,

02:19:59.040 --> 02:20:00.628
tomorrow you will hear him.

02:20:02.482 --> 02:20:07.142
The next day, Grippa and Bernice came with
great pomp and entered the audience room

02:20:07.142 --> 02:20:11.390
with the high -ranking military officers
and the prominent men of the city.

02:20:11.390 --> 02:20:13.910
At the command of Festus, Paul was brought
in.

02:20:13.910 --> 02:20:17.930
Festus said, King Agrippa and all who are
present with us, you see this man.

02:20:17.930 --> 02:20:21.710
The whole Jewish community has petitioned
me about him in Jerusalem and here in

02:20:21.710 --> 02:20:22.410
Caesarea,

02:20:22.710 --> 02:20:24.970
shouting that he ought not to live any
longer.

02:20:24.970 --> 02:20:28.290
I found that he has done nothing deserving
of death, but because he made his appeal

02:20:28.290 --> 02:20:30.996
to the emperor, I decided to send him to
Rome.

02:20:31.150 --> 02:20:34.670
But I have nothing definite to write to
his majesty about him.

02:20:34.670 --> 02:20:37.410
Therefore, I have brought him before all
of you

02:20:37.410 --> 02:20:42.110
King Agrippa, so that as a result of this
investigation I may have something to

02:20:42.110 --> 02:20:47.950
write sent to

02:20:48.030 --> 02:20:52.070
Paul. You have permission to speak for
yourself.

02:20:52.530 --> 02:20:55.390
So Paul motioned with his hand and began
his defense.

02:20:55.390 --> 02:21:00.970
King Agrippa, I consider myself fortunate
to stand before you today as I make my

02:21:00.970 --> 02:21:05.450
defense against all the accusations of the
Jews, and especially so because you are

02:21:05.450 --> 02:21:08.930
well acquainted and with all the Jewish
customs and controversies.

02:21:08.930 --> 02:21:11.170
Therefore, I beg you to listen to me
patiently.

02:21:11.170 --> 02:21:15.750
The Jewish people all know the way I have
lived ever since I was a child, from the

02:21:15.750 --> 02:21:18.870
the beginning of my life in my own country
and also Jerusalem.

02:21:18.870 --> 02:21:22.390
They have known me for a long time to
testify if they are willing, that I

02:21:22.390 --> 02:21:26.450
conform to the strictest sect of our
religion, living as a Pharisee.

02:21:26.590 --> 02:21:30.750
And now it is because of my hope in God
has promised our ancestors that I am on

02:21:30.750 --> 02:21:35.050
trial today. This is the promise our 12
tribes are hoping to seek fulfilled as

02:21:35.050 --> 02:21:37.344
they earnestly serve God day and night.

02:21:37.590 --> 02:21:41.570
King Agrippa, it is because of his hope
that these Jews are accusing me.

02:21:41.570 --> 02:21:45.210
Why should any of you consider it
incredible that God raises the dead?

02:21:45.210 --> 02:21:49.610
I too was convinced that I ought to do all
that was possible to oppose the name of

02:21:49.610 --> 02:21:52.786
Jesus of Nazareth. and that's what I did
in Jerusalem.

02:21:52.850 --> 02:21:56.810
On the authority of the chief priest, I
put many of the Lord's people in prison

02:21:56.810 --> 02:21:59.870
and when they were put to death, I cast my
vote against them.

02:21:59.870 --> 02:22:03.988
Many a time I went from one synagogue to
another to have them punished

02:22:04.590 --> 02:22:09.010
to blaspheme. I was so obsessed with
persecuting them that I even hunted them

02:22:09.010 --> 02:22:13.290
down in foreign cities. On one of these
journeys, I was going to Damascus with the

02:22:13.290 --> 02:22:15.550
authority and commission of chief priests.

02:22:15.550 --> 02:22:19.670
About noon, King Agrippa, as I was on the
road, I saw a light from heaven, brighter

02:22:19.670 --> 02:22:21.490
than the sun blazing around me

02:22:22.050 --> 02:22:26.250
and my companions. We all fell to the
ground and I heard a voice saying to me in

02:22:26.250 --> 02:22:28.897
Aramaic, Saul, Saul, why do you persecute
me?

02:22:28.970 --> 02:22:31.970
It is hard for you to kick against the
goats.

02:22:32.900 --> 02:22:34.440
Then I asked, who are you, Lord?

02:22:34.440 --> 02:22:37.740
I am Jesus whom you are persecuting, the
Lord replied.

02:22:38.000 --> 02:22:40.000
Now get up and stand on your feet.

02:22:40.160 --> 02:22:43.740
I have appeared to you to appoint you as a
servant and as a witness of what you have

02:22:43.740 --> 02:22:45.260
seen and will see of me.

02:22:45.540 --> 02:22:48.400
I will rescue you from your own people and
from the Gentiles.

02:22:48.400 --> 02:22:52.220
I am sending you to them to open their
eyes and turn from darkness to light and

02:22:52.220 --> 02:22:56.320
with the power of Satan to God so that
they may receive forgiveness of sins and

02:22:56.320 --> 02:22:59.340
among those who are sanctified by faith in
me.

02:22:59.880 --> 02:23:02.860
So then, King Agrippa, I was not
disobedient to the vision from heaven.

02:23:02.860 --> 02:23:07.020
First to those in Damascus, then to those
in Jerusalem and all of Judea and to the

02:23:07.020 --> 02:23:11.160
Gentiles, I preached that they should
repent and turn to God and demonstrate

02:23:11.160 --> 02:23:13.042
their repentance by their deeds.

02:23:13.120 --> 02:23:16.960
That is why some Jews seized me in the
temple courts and tried to kill me.

02:23:16.960 --> 02:23:18.840
But God has helped me to this very day.

02:23:18.840 --> 02:23:21.958
So I stand here and testify to small and
great alike.

02:23:22.120 --> 02:23:25.360
I am saying nothing beyond what the
prophets and Moses said would happen, that

02:23:25.360 --> 02:23:29.480
the Messiah would suffer and as the first
to rise from the dead, but would bring the

02:23:29.480 --> 02:23:32.020
message of light to his own people and to
the Gentiles.

02:23:32.020 --> 02:23:35.060
At this point, Thestas interrupted Paul's
defense.

02:23:35.520 --> 02:23:38.049
You are out of your mind, Paul, he
shouted.

02:23:38.360 --> 02:23:40.860
Your great learning is driving you insane.

02:23:41.720 --> 02:23:45.280
I am not insane, most excellent Thestas,
Paul replied.

02:23:45.620 --> 02:23:47.660
What I'm saying is true and reasonable.

02:23:47.660 --> 02:23:51.000
The king is familiar with all of these
things and I can speak freely to him.

02:23:51.000 --> 02:23:54.080
I am convinced that none of this has
escaped his notice because, because it was

02:23:54.080 --> 02:23:57.520
not done in a corner. King Agripp, do you
believe the prophets?

02:23:57.520 --> 02:24:01.800
I know you do. Then Agrippa said to Paul,
do you think that in such a short time you

02:24:01.800 --> 02:24:03.800
can persuade me to be a Christian?

02:24:03.940 --> 02:24:05.881
Paul replied, short time or long.

02:24:05.900 --> 02:24:11.550
I pray to God, not only you, but all who
are listening to me, may today and may

02:24:11.550 --> 02:24:13.962
become what I am except for these chains.

02:24:14.030 --> 02:24:18.750
The king arose and with him, the governor
and Bernice and those sitting with them,

02:24:18.750 --> 02:24:22.250
after they left the room they began saying
to one another, this man is not doing

02:24:22.250 --> 02:24:24.897
anything that deserves death or
imprisonment.

02:24:26.380 --> 02:24:27.620
Paul replied,

02:24:28.560 --> 02:24:30.600
short time or long. I pray to God,

02:24:37.080 --> 02:24:40.040
not only you, but we would sail for Italy.

02:24:40.600 --> 02:24:45.420
Paul and some of the other prisoners were
handed over to a centurion named Julius,

02:24:45.420 --> 02:24:47.860
who belonged to the imperial regiment.

02:24:53.266 --> 02:24:58.366
about to sail for ports along the coast of
the province of Asia, and we set out to

02:24:58.366 --> 02:24:59.066
see.

02:24:59.646 --> 02:25:02.999
Aristarchus, a Macedonian from
Thessalonica, was with us.

02:25:03.456 --> 02:25:07.496
The next day, we landed at Sida, and
Julius, in his kindness to Paul, allowed

02:25:07.496 --> 02:25:12.830
him to go to his friends, so then that
they might provide for his needs.

02:25:13.290 --> 02:25:19.720
From there, we put out to sea again and
pass to the pass to

02:25:19.720 --> 02:25:20.720
the Lee of Cyprus

02:25:21.240 --> 02:25:23.240
because the winds were against us.

02:25:23.500 --> 02:25:29.580
When we had sailed across the open ocean
off the coast of Cilicia and

02:25:29.580 --> 02:25:32.780
Pamphylia, we landed in Myra and Lycia.

02:25:34.100 --> 02:25:40.060
Then there, the centurion found an
Alexandria ship sailing for Italy and put

02:25:40.060 --> 02:25:40.766
us on board.

02:25:41.380 --> 02:25:45.860
We made slow headway for many days and had
difficulty arriving

02:25:46.420 --> 02:25:47.538
arriving in Naitis.

02:25:49.190 --> 02:25:54.110
When the wind did not allow us to hold our
course, we sailed to the Lee of Crete,

02:25:54.110 --> 02:25:55.470
opposite the Solomon.

02:25:56.900 --> 02:26:01.920
We moved past the coast with difficulty
and came to a place called Fair Heavens

02:26:01.920 --> 02:26:03.332
near the town of Lascia.

02:26:04.190 --> 02:26:09.169
Much time had been lost and sailing had
already become dangerous because by now it

02:26:09.169 --> 02:26:12.670
was after the Day of Atonement and so Paul
worn them.

02:26:13.470 --> 02:26:18.190
Men, I can see that our voyage is going to
be disastrous and bring great loss to ship

02:26:18.190 --> 02:26:20.850
and cargo and to our own lives also.

02:26:21.460 --> 02:26:24.872
But the centurion, instead of listening to
what Paul said,

02:26:25.470 --> 02:26:28.790
followed the advice of the pilot and the
owner of the ship.

02:26:28.790 --> 02:26:33.290
Since the harbor was unsuitable to winter
in, the majority decided that we should

02:26:33.290 --> 02:26:36.530
sail on, hoping to reach Phoenix and
winter there.

02:26:37.630 --> 02:26:41.510
This was a harboring creek facing both
southwest and northwest.

02:26:43.210 --> 02:26:46.460
When the gentle south wind began to blow,

02:26:47.040 --> 02:26:49.020
they saw their opportunity.

02:26:49.020 --> 02:26:53.540
So they weighed the anchor and sailed
along the shore of Crete.

02:26:53.880 --> 02:26:59.030
Before very long, the wind of hurricane
forest called the Northeaster

02:26:59.710 --> 02:27:01.181
swept up from the island.

02:27:01.490 --> 02:27:05.314
The ship was caught by the wind and could
not head into the wind.

02:27:05.350 --> 02:27:09.910
So we gave away to it and were driven
along.

02:27:10.790 --> 02:27:14.310
As we passed the lee of a small island
called Cadia,

02:27:14.870 --> 02:27:16.811
we were heartily able to make it,

02:27:17.590 --> 02:27:19.130
make the lifeboat secure.

02:27:19.550 --> 02:27:21.370
So the men hoisted it aboard.

02:27:22.260 --> 02:27:26.820
Then they passed the ropes under the ship
itself to hold it together.

02:27:27.480 --> 02:27:32.960
Because they were afraid they would run
aground on the Sambor's service,

02:27:34.310 --> 02:27:37.630
they lowered the sea anchor and let the
ship be driven along.

02:27:37.630 --> 02:27:42.580
We took such a violent battering from the
storm that the next day day, they began to

02:27:42.580 --> 02:27:43.940
throw cargo overboard.

02:27:44.770 --> 02:27:49.358
On the third day, they threw the ship's
tackle overboard with their own hands.

02:27:49.450 --> 02:27:54.890
When neither sun nor stars appeared for
many days and the storm continued raging,

02:27:55.410 --> 02:27:58.175
we finally gave up all hope out of being
saved.

02:27:59.260 --> 02:28:04.750
After they had gone a long time without
food, Paul stood up before them and said,

02:28:05.350 --> 02:28:08.730
man, you should have taken my advice not
to sail from Crete.

02:28:08.730 --> 02:28:12.310
Then you would have been spared yourself
this damage and loss.

02:28:12.310 --> 02:28:16.630
But now I urge you to keep up your courage
because not one of you will be lost.

02:28:16.630 --> 02:28:18.512
Only the ship will be destroyed.

02:28:18.730 --> 02:28:25.010
Last night, an angel of the God who I
belong to and whom I serve stood beside me

02:28:25.010 --> 02:28:26.951
and said, do not be afraid, Paul.

02:28:27.110 --> 02:28:32.410
You must stand trial before Caesar and God
that has graciously given you all the

02:28:32.410 --> 02:28:34.234
lives of all who sail with you.

02:28:34.740 --> 02:28:38.913
So keep your courage, man, for I have
faith in God that it will happen just as

02:28:38.913 --> 02:28:42.501
he told me. Nevertheless, we must run
aground on some island.

02:28:43.634 --> 02:28:47.914
On the 14th night, we were still being
driven across the Adriatic Sea.

02:28:48.864 --> 02:28:52.805
When about midnight, the sailors sensed
they were approaching land.

02:28:58.676 --> 02:29:03.416
A short time later they took soundings
again and found that it was 90 bd.

02:29:08.120 --> 02:29:12.860
just as he told me. In an attempt to
escape from the ship,

02:29:13.500 --> 02:29:17.580
the sailors let the lifeboat down into the
sea, pretending they were going to lower

02:29:17.580 --> 02:29:19.521
some of the anchors from the bow.

02:29:19.920 --> 02:29:24.180
Then Paul said to the centurion and the
soldiers, unless these men stay with.

02:29:24.180 --> 02:29:25.886
The ship you cannot be saved.

02:29:26.400 --> 02:29:30.500
So the soldiers cut the ropes that held
the lifeboat and let it drift away.

02:29:30.500 --> 02:29:33.540
Just before dawn, Paul urged all of them
to eat.

02:29:34.120 --> 02:29:38.340
For the last 14 days, he said you have
been in constant suspense

02:29:39.100 --> 02:29:40.740
and have gone without food.

02:29:40.740 --> 02:29:43.190
You haven't eaten anything.

02:29:43.810 --> 02:29:45.751
Now I urge you to take some food.

02:29:46.270 --> 02:29:47.682
You need it to survive.,

02:29:48.150 --> 02:29:51.190
not one of you will lose a single hair
from his head.

02:29:51.190 --> 02:29:55.970
After he said this, he took some bread and
gave thanks to God in front of all.

02:29:57.480 --> 02:29:59.480
Then he broke it and began to eat.

02:30:00.250 --> 02:30:03.426
They were all encouraged and ate some food
themselves.

02:30:03.710 --> 02:30:06.590
Although there were 276 of us on board,

02:30:07.760 --> 02:30:12.420
when they had eaten as much as they
wanted, they liked the ship by throwing

02:30:12.420 --> 02:30:13.773
the grain into the sea.

02:30:14.450 --> 02:30:19.590
When daylight came, they did not recognize
the land, but they saw a bay with a sandy

02:30:19.590 --> 02:30:23.296
beach where they decided to run the ship
aground if they could.

02:30:23.510 --> 02:30:28.350
Cutting loose the anchors, they left them
in the sea and at the same time, untied

02:30:28.350 --> 02:30:30.232
the ropes that held the rudders.

02:30:30.770 --> 02:30:35.990
Then they hoisted the foresail to the wind
and made for the beach, but the ship

02:30:36.550 --> 02:30:38.810
struck a sandbar and ran aground.

02:30:39.550 --> 02:30:43.590
The bow struck past and would not move,
and the stern was broken to pieces by the

02:30:43.590 --> 02:30:44.825
pounding of the surf.

02:30:45.200 --> 02:30:48.920
The soldiers planned to kill the prisoners
to prevent any of them from swimming away

02:30:48.920 --> 02:30:54.240
and escaping, but the centurion wanted to
spare Paul's life and kept them from

02:30:54.240 --> 02:30:55.652
carrying out their plan.

02:30:56.360 --> 02:31:00.960
He ordered those who could swing to jump
overboard for us and get to land.

02:31:01.890 --> 02:31:02.790
The rest were

02:31:03.780 --> 02:31:07.020
to get there on planes or other pieces of
the ship.

02:31:07.420 --> 02:31:10.080
This way, everyone reached the land
safely.

02:31:14.820 --> 02:31:19.232
Once we were safe on shore, we learned
that we were on the island of Malta.

02:31:19.920 --> 02:31:22.460
The people of the island were very kind to
us.

02:31:22.460 --> 02:31:26.636
It was cold and rainy, so they built a
fire on the shore to welcome us.

02:31:27.100 --> 02:31:31.240
As Paul gathered an armful of sticks and
was laying them on the fire, a poisonous

02:31:31.240 --> 02:31:34.490
snake,, driven out by the heat, bit him on
the hand.

02:31:35.300 --> 02:31:39.240
The people of the island saw it hanging
from his hand and said to each other, a

02:31:39.240 --> 02:31:40.358
murderer, no doubt.

02:31:40.820 --> 02:31:44.526
Though he escaped the sea, justice will
not permit him to live.

02:31:44.830 --> 02:31:48.359
But Paul shook off the snake into the fire
and was unharmed.

02:31:49.200 --> 02:31:52.729
The people waited for him to swell up or
suddenly drop dead.

02:31:53.330 --> 02:31:57.830
But when they had waited a long time and
saw that he wasn't harmed, they changed

02:31:57.830 --> 02:32:00.006
their minds and decided he was a god.

02:32:00.960 --> 02:32:01.842
Near the shore,

02:32:02.660 --> 02:32:07.480
where we landed, was an estate, belonging
to Publius, the chief, chief official of

02:32:07.480 --> 02:32:11.598
the island. He welcomed us and treated us
kindly for three days, days.

02:32:11.620 --> 02:32:15.800
As it happened, Publius' father was ill
with fever and dysentery.

02:32:16.860 --> 02:32:21.200
Paul went in and prayed for him and laying
his hands on him, he healed him.

02:32:21.200 --> 02:32:25.082
Then all the other sick people on the
island came and were healed.

02:32:25.740 --> 02:32:28.211
As a result, we were showered with honors.

02:32:28.280 --> 02:32:32.200
And when the time came to sail, people
supplied us with everything we would need

02:32:32.200 --> 02:32:32.965
for the trip.

02:32:34.870 --> 02:32:39.570
It was three months after the shipwreck
that we set sail on another ship that had

02:32:39.570 --> 02:32:45.110
wintered at the island, an Alexandrian
ship with the twin gods as its figurehead.

02:32:46.270 --> 02:32:48.310
Our first stop was Syracuse,

02:32:49.230 --> 02:32:51.170
where we stayed three days.

02:32:52.750 --> 02:32:55.050
From there we sailed across to Regium.

02:32:56.020 --> 02:32:59.526
A day later, Later, a south wind began
blowing, so the following day, we sailed

02:32:59.526 --> 02:33:01.486
up the coast to Putole.

02:33:02.290 --> 02:33:06.110
There we found some believers who invited
us to spend a week with with them and so

02:33:06.110 --> 02:33:06.810
we came.

02:33:08.626 --> 02:33:12.626
The brothers and sisters in Rome had heard
we were coming, and they—

02:33:12.722 --> 02:33:15.882
came to meet us at the forum on the Apian
Way.

02:33:18.860 --> 02:33:20.220
a When

02:33:21.130 --> 02:33:24.012
Paul saw them, he was encouraged and
thanked God.

02:33:26.860 --> 02:33:28.272
When we arrived in Rome,

02:33:28.740 --> 02:33:32.680
Paul was permitted to have his own private
lodging though he was guarded by a

02:33:32.680 --> 02:33:33.380
